---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH

#### 1. Conditional Test Logic — `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 31)

```csharp
if (result.TotalAmount > 100)
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
```

One branch never executes — you silently skip verification of either the premium or standard path.

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_SmallOrder_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-CHEAP", 1) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_LargeOrder_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One code path is never tested; a regression there goes undetected.

---

#### 2. Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 44)

```csharp
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
// nothing asserted
```

This passes even if every field on the result is wrong — it only fails on an unhandled exception.

**Fix — assert the expected outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);

    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage is counted but nothing is verified.

---

#### 3. Sleepy Test — `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` (line 98)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(2000);
```

A hard 2-second sleep. Too short on a slow CI runner → flaky false failure. Always slow everywhere else.

**Fix — poll with a timeout or use a synchronization primitive:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);

    // FakeEmailSender exposes a wait handle or an async completion source
    var sent = await _email.WaitForNotificationAsync(order.Id, timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
